<p>French President Emmanuel Macron will visit Cyprus on Monday for talks with Cypriot President Nikos Christodoulides and Greek Prime Minister Kyriakos Mitsotakis, as France sends warships to the Mediterranean after a drone attack on the EU member island. Paris says the trip is meant to bolster security around Cyprus and the eastern Mediterranean, as the regional escalation involving the United States, Israel and Iran ripples across the Middle East.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Fju0OtqtOYKPdzbhfJRtNLz97XhzLAuy--7unPtRnIFxSrUplJDXczhWdcAgF-kCyeiwCY42s_18cxZHAK8twbVTS4L8XQUMX-W8iD563WWzqg0L2Te5X70ZUYjXytUX8DJkj6wWc5eyyVmvLXj7nQWgielhYln0NEGbw9bqd3MNOjkH' alt='French President Emmanuel Macron gestures before greeting the president of Singapore at the Elysée Palace in Paris on March 3, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Élysée Palace (France): France cast Macron’s trip as a show of “solidarity” and said he would lay out steps to strengthen security around Cyprus and in the eastern Mediterranean. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3345905/macron-visit-cyprus-france-deploys-warships-mediterranean'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>Élysée Palace (France): French officials tied the visit and naval deployments to the wider regional escalation, saying the conflict involving the US, Israel and Iran is affecting much of the Middle East. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/macron-visit-cyprus-french-warships-deploy-counter-iran-threat'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Le Monde: Le Monde reported that Macron ordered the Charles de Gaulle aircraft carrier deployed to the Mediterranean after the drone strike on Cyprus. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/middle-east-crisis/article/2026/03/08/macron-to-visit-cyprus-after-drone-attack-on-the-island-eu-member_6751220_368.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3345905/macron-visit-cyprus-france-deploys-warships-mediterranean'>Mac